C. OWN-SURFACE BUG FOUND + FIXED (caught by the integration build / isolated test run)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Type-name collision: my chip-flow view was named `FlowChips`, colliding with the
   existing `FleetApiSection.Onboarding.swift` `FlowChips`. Renamed mine to
   `NLSqlPlaygroundTableChipFlow` (all other surface types already NLSqlPlayground-prefixed).
2. Actor-isolation: the `InMemoryNLSqlPlaygroundSource.envelope(for:)` pure JSON encoder was
   @MainActor-isolated (class is @MainActor), which a nonisolated test helper could not call
   under Swift 6 strict concurrency. Marked it `nonisolated` (it touches no actor state).
   The isolated `swift test` then ran 56/56 green.

